This paper focuses on three key types of oscillatory integrals: 
1) those with smooth phases that are restricted to a two-dimensional manifold;
2) those with non-smooth phases that are restricted to a two-dimensional manifold;
3) those with smooth phases that are unbounded.

We derive estimates for the first two categories using methods similar to those in a recent paper by Stefanos Karachalios and Kevin Roth. For the third type, we derive estimates in an intrinsic space related to the polynomial growth of the phase and demonstrate their application in deriving bounds for the Sobolev space norms of specific functions related to the oscillatory integral.
